roaden an identity check.\\n\\nCheckout configuration is process command-scope only. The three keys are forbidden at workflow/job scope, in `GITHUB_ENV`, in later step env maps, and in any diagnostic owned child. No global/system/local/worktree config write, extra command, short-path relocation, sparse checkout, omitted archive, permission/Secrets change, retry, native probe or version query is admitted. The JSON checkout input map, ordered commands, required synthetic controls and all upload/schema/provenance rules remain unchanged. Existing sourceFiles still contains exactly eleven paths; its current hashes and the strict bindingHash check must match the new exact candidate.\\n\\nFresh independent supporting pre-scope and actual-diff reviews must inspect both binding documents and the two identity literals. Checkout env confinement requires separate static positive/negative supporting controls: the existing synthetic suite does not itself lock this env map. Do not change its source or required_future_controls to manufacture coverage. Independent different-model-family supporting acceptance and an explicit Coordinator publication/execution ruling are required before one new exact-source INITIAL workflow opportunity on the already-locked non-main branch; no automatic retries or native environment repair. Preserve the original failure run, all old originals, historical inventories and frozen files. Checkout success alone is not INITIAL observation completeness, product acceptance, F005 or release readiness.\\n\",\n142\t    \"cli_identity_replacements\": [\n143\t      {\"constant\":\"bindingHash\",\"old\":\"ed24ebf3b4b1890f84f09ba82edd0d71f75a12e35504a84a3fb0f9d8300455fc\",\"new_rule\":\"SHA-256 of revised BL-WINDOWS-P1-INITIAL-BINDINGS-20261010.json\"},\n144\t      {\"constant\":\"mdHash\",\"old\":\"bf60ca426602d00b76515091cc30abd37badea21731b6ad21fe54cd323d7577c\",\"new_rule\":\"SHA-256 of revised BL-WINDOWS-P1-INITIAL-BINDINGS-20261010.md\"}\n145\t    ],\n146\t    