osal and four-path/identity exception before Generator work.\",\n204\t      \"Later Generator creates minimal candidate in its isolated workspace without push or production/state work, with exact paths, parent SHA, diff and hashes.\",\n205\t      \"Fresh independent actual-diff scope critic accepts exact C and revised bindings. A separate fresh supporting Evaluator from a different model_family than Generator executes offline/negative and existing synthetic acceptance, writing original full outputs/verdict; Planner/Generator/Coordinator do not rewrite it.\",\n206\t      \"Only after accepted exact C, Coordinator obtains and records separate explicit non-main publication plus one INITIAL execution authority; worker never pushes and machine never writes pending_gate.decision.\",\n207\t      \"New native run is independently evaluated on captured bytes and exact C; report release_ready=false and formal_F005_claim=false regardless of checkout success. No auto-release or native environment repair.\"\n208\t    ],\n209\t    \"null_is_not_authority\": true\n210\t  },\n211\t  \"performed_by_this_planner\": {\n212\t    \"disk_original_hashes_and_json_log_reconciliation\": true,\n213\t    \"source_and_frozen_hash_checks\": true,\n214\t    \"git_tree_path_inventory\": true,\n215\t    \"validator_and_env_test_static_read\": true,\n216\t    \"official_primary_documentation_browse\": true,\n217\t    \"in_memory_delta_consistency_check\": true,\n218\t    \"source_implementation\": false,\n219\t    \"test_suite_execution\": false,\n220\t    \"dependency_install\": false,\n221\t    \"native_execution\": false,\n222\t    \"ci_trigger_or_rerun\": false,\n223\t    \"push_or_deploy\": false,\n224\t    \"main_prod_or_backup_keys_access\": false,\n225\t    \"state_gate_or_memory_edits\": false,\n226\t    \"parent_worktree_index_write\": false,\n227\t    \"git_config_write\": false\n228\t  },\n229\t  \"remaining_boundaries\": [\"checkout Windows feasibility unverified\",\"native INITIAL execution/provenance/environment cause unverified\",\"native environment repair not authorized\",\"main/production untouched\",\"backup keys/off-host backup gates unresolved\",\"Compose HARD_STOP unresolved\",\"F004/F005/release gates unresolved\",\"whole-process-tree absence unproved\"],\n230\t  \"primary_references\": [\n231\t    {\"url\":\"https://git-scm.com/docs/git-config/2.55.0#Documentation/git-config.txt-GITCONFIGCOUNT\",\"supports\":\"zero-indexed GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/KEY_n/VALUE_n runtime config; file overrides and explicit -c precedence; missing key/value errors\"},\n232\t    {\"url\":\"https://github.com/git-for-windows/git/blob/v2.55.0.windows.5/Documentation/config/core.adoc\",\"supports\":\"core.longpaths supports Git for Windows builtins; not a general Windows/npm/PowerShell repair\"},\n233\t    {\"url\":\"https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/workflow-syntax#jobsjob_idstepsenv\",\"supports\":\"step environment scope, distinct from job/workflow scope\"},\n234\t    {\"url\":\"https://github.com/actions/checkout/blob/11d5960a326750d5838078e36cf38b85af677262/src/git-command-manager.ts\",\"supports\":\"execGit copies process.env into Git child env before action-owned overrides; observed action source has no GIT_CONFIG_COUNT/KEY_0/VALUE_0 overwrite\"},\n235\t    {\"url\":\"https://github.com/actions/checkout/blob/11d5960a326750d5838078e36cf38b85af677262/README.md\",\"supports\":\"path relative under GITHUB_WORKSPACE; sparse materialization; persist-credentials input\"}\n236\t  ]\n237\t}"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_dZStivXTgzuvroOs5pZ0OhHF","content":"1\t# Windows P1 checkout-only successor proposal\n2\t\n3\tFresh supporting Planner, `harness-rules.md` section 1.5. Exact source:\n4\t`888a5acd7a8a441c9ec4ad898453f149cf8d6b7c` (tree\n5\t`19186fe317bce76857dc273a9c21b3e940da9e41`). Created 2026-10-11 UTC.\n6\t\n7\t**Proposal only.** Neither implementation, publication, CI/native execution,\n8\tnative environment repair, state transition nor release is authorized here.\n9\t`release_ready=false`, `release_acceptance=false`, `formal_F005_claim=false`.\n10\tNo branch is pushed. `main`, production, credentials and backup keys are untouched.\n11\tCompose HARD_STOP, F004/F005 and release gates remain unresolved.\n12\t\n13\t## Verified first failure, not a native result\n14\t\n15\tRead directly from the four original run files under:\n16\t\n17\t`/Volumes/ORICO/project/.worktrees/tokenizer-release-readiness-20261008/docs/test-reports/BL-RELEASE-READINESS-coordination-20261011/`\n18\t\n19\t- Run **38145284914**, attempt 1, job **114487223393**, exact source888,\n20\t  push to `codex/windows-p1-stages-ci-20261010`: completed/failure.\n21\t- First failed step: `actions/checkout@v4`, Git exit **128**. Full original log\n22\t  lines 89-90 contain checkout of source888 followed by `Filename too long`.\n23\t  The action resolved to `11d5960a326750d5838078e36cf38b85af677262`; Git was\n24\t  `2.55.0.windows.5`; workspace was `D:\\a\\tokenizer\\tokenizer`.\n25\t- `setup-node`, prepare, `npm ci`, synthetic checks and INITIAL were **skipped**.\n26\t  The always-seal step then failed with `MODULE_NOT_FOUND` for `p1-stages.mjs`\n27\t  (lines 110/118). This is a secondary incomplete-checkout failure, not an\n28\t  independently reached diagnostic defect. Verify/upload were skipped.\n29\t- Original artifact API response: **0 artifacts**. Do not fabricate a typed\n30\t  summary, native case verdict, sealed evidence, whole-tree absence or a product\n31\t  PASS from these logs. No INITIAL admission was observed because its step was\n32\t  skipped; workflow orchestration shells are not INITIAL native admissions.\n33\t\n34\t| Original filename suffix after `windows-initial-native-run38145284914-` | Bytes | SHA-256 |\n35\t| --- | ---: | --- |\n36\t| `final-original.json` | 12339 | `a801a6dbda7f2eed3cc7be6280830540b5cc20e3fae04472e0c0085a5666c3ad` |\n37\t| `jobs-original.json` | 2944 | `4320e6204f4ea41da2aec74e436cb229c8d9793f6070306e6c576b1cd9a13d44` |\n38\t| `artifacts-original.json` | 32 | `244563f989470892c537c9a4622920af0d228ee4528f7d00c64a06d6cd95856c` |\n39\t| `full-original.log` | 18378 | `725070982a434eb7421b339d6fc5886d76f7f7a631a4a381a9c95a79bcbdcd8e` |\n40\t\n41\tThe full log has 137 lines. It was not truncated, shortened or copied into this\n42\tplan. Original bytes remain at their original paths.\n43\t\n44\t## Path and source evidence\n45\t\n46\tThe failed directory is:\n47\t\n48\t```text\n49\tdocs/test-reports/windows-native-ci-20261008/runtime-parity-run-37822555762-original/windows-release-diagnostics-719c2df0d54f62b1b3b3e711a2045ffd8ea5e711/windows-release-diagnosis-20261008/native-output-parity-1791483248698\n50\t```\n51\t\n52\t`git -c core.fileMode=false ls-tree -rz --full-tree source888` has 2453 tracked\n53\tpaths; raw NUL-delimited inventory SHA-256 is\n54\t`af29538927397b7ec48c261ca047616d9a18617a65f767165b61105d396d1a23`.\n55\tAt the logged workspace prefix (25 characters including separator), all 55 files\n56\tbelow that directory have Windows absolute lengths **265-281**. The directory\n57\titself is 248 characters; the logged directory-level error does not mean that\n58\tdirectory itself is above 260. The longest tracked relative path is 256\n59\tcharacters, ending in `downstream-off-confirmation.json`, blob\n60\t`a3d877dca98202f202013de02e6731f026432da8`.\n61\t\n62\tThe failed-subtree inventory SHA-256 is\n63\t`6cd55acce1fcd1a225edb9e96c2444c5f3a20f3ae38aaf3a6a2ffa1a78ac902f`.\n64\tThe enclosing current git archive root has **57** tracked entries, inventory\n65\t`52ac3b835b45e6aa3c54ea72f57180421822c5719d2a9e9bca0d2abbbf0a0721`.\n66\tThese current git-tree counts are **not** the historical 59-file runtime\n67\tfilesystem inventory. No old 59/57 archive or inventory is rewritten or treated\n68\tas freshly authenticated native evidence. All ten referenced frozen/prior source\n69\thashes match the locked JSON; their exact paths and hashes are in `proposal.json`.\n70\t\n71\t## One selected solution: only checkout-step runtime Git configuration\n72\t\n73\tAdd exactly four lines to the existing checkout step:\n74\t\n75\t```diff\n76\t       - uses: actions/checkout@v4\n77\t+        env:\n78\t+          GIT_CONFIG_COUNT: '1'\n79\t+          GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0: core.longpaths\n80\t+          GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0: 'true'\n81\t         with:\n82\t           ref: ${{ github.sha }}\n83\t           fetch-depth: 1\n84\t           persist-credentials: false\n85\t```\n86\t\n87\t**Every other workflow byte stays unchanged.** No new shell step, native child,\n88\tversion query, retry, checkout path, sparse/filter input, permission, Secret,\n89\tevent/ref, default working directory, timeout, CLI mode or upload change.\n90\t\n91\tGit documents these zero-indexed environment pairs as process-runtime config;\n92\tthey override config-file values, while explicit `git -c` still takes precedence.\n93\tThis avoids a persistent config mutation. See the\n94\t[Git 2.55 configuration environment contract](https://git-scm.com/docs/git-config/2.55.0#Documentation/git-config.txt-GITCONFIGCOUNT).\n95\t\n96\t`core.longpaths` is Git for Windows builtin-command support, not a general\n97\tWindows or native-toolchain repair. See the\n98\t[observed Git for Windows version's core configuration](https://github.com/git-for-windows/git/blob/v2.55.0.windows.5/Documentation/config/core.adoc).\n99\tGitHub documents step-local environment scope, distinct from workflow/job env:\n100\t[workflow step env](https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/workflows-and-actions/workflow-syntax#jobsjob_idstepsenv).\n101\t\n102\tThe observed checkout action's `execGit` copies `process.env` into its child\n103\tenvironment, then applies its own overrides; the inspected source does not\n104\toverwrite the three chosen config keys. See\n105\t[the exact resolved checkout implementation](https://github.com/actions/checkout/blob/11d5960a326750d5838078e36cf38b85af677262/src/git-command-manager.ts).\n106\t**Inference:** the proposed step keys should reach the checkout Git builtin and\n107\taddress this observed layer without changing native E0. This is documented\n108\tcandidate feasibility, **not a performed Windows checkout**. A changed resolved\n109\t`v4` action must be independently inspected; no silent upgrade/pinning is included.\n110\t\n111\tThe three keys are prohibited at workflow/job scope, in `GITHUB_ENV`, in every\n112\tlater step, and in owned diagnostic children. The existing CLI reconstructs E0\n113\tfrom exactly five admitted system keys plus its fixed synthetic keys, rather than\n114\tspreading the runner environment. `GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1`, an owned empty global\n115\tconfig and strict guard key equality stay unchanged. Checkout configuration does\n116\tnot authorize `APPDATA`, `LOCALAPPDATA`, `SystemDrive`, `PSModulePath`, additional\n117\tselectors, a command fallback or any PowerShell environment repair.\n118\t\n119\t### Alternatives compared, not authorized\n120\t\n121\t| Alternative | Why it is broader or weaker here |\n122\t| --- | --- |\n123\t| Direct `git -c core.longpaths=true` | Narrow scope, but action-owned argv would require wrapping/replacing checkout. |\n124\t| `--global` | Adds persistent user config and a shell step; logged action temporarily changes HOME for global operations. |\n125\t| `--system` | Machine scope and possible privilege requirement, unnecessary for a per-action setting. |\n126\t| `--local` / `--worktree` | Repository does not yet exist; setting after checkout is too late; custom init/config introduces state. |\n127\t| Short checkout `path` | Action path is relative **under** already-long `GITHUB_WORKSPACE`; a child path does not shorten it. |\n128\t| Custom short root / `subst` | Relocation, working-directory/upload rewrites or host state perturb provenance. |\n129\t| Sparse checkout | Omits old archives and changes the full materialized source/evidence contract. |\n130\t| OS policy switch / retries | Host-wide repair or repeated execution is not checkout-only scope. |\n131\t\n132\tPath/sparse semantics are documented in the\n133\t[exact checkout action README](https://github.com/actions/checkout/blob/11d5960a326750d5838078e36cf38b85af677262/README.md).\n134\tDo not delete, move, rewrite or omit historical artifacts to avoid the path error.\n135\t\n136\t## Required explicit contract revision: four files, not hidden permission\n137\t\n138\tThe current binding documents only permit three **new** INITIAL files and say\n139\t`existing_file_edits_allowed=[]`. Those files now exist. A workflow-only fix would\n140\tcontradict that contract. This proposal therefore requests a fresh C001 scope\n141\truling before any edits, not silent reliance on the earlier INITIAL acceptance.\n142\t\n143\tThe later Generator allowlist is exactly:\n144\t\n145\t1. `.github/workflows/windows-p1-stages-diagnostic.yml`: the four-line env delta.\n146\t2. `docs/specs/BL-WINDOWS-P1-INITIAL-BINDINGS-20261010.md`: append only the exact\n147\t   C001 section held in `proposal.json`; prior text remains intact. The appendix\n148\t   explicitly supersedes only the additions-only existing-file prohibition.\n149\t3. `docs/specs/BL-WINDOWS-P1-INITIAL-BINDINGS-20261010.json`: exactly five unique\n150\t   byte substitutions specified in `proposal.json`:\n151\t   - revision `1 -> 2`;\n152\t   - updated timestamp `2026-10-11T05:49:43Z -> 2026-10-11T14:04:39Z`;\n153\t   - revision scope `B001-only -> C001 checkout-only exception, B001 unchanged`;\n154\t   - empty existing-file allowlist -> these exact four paths;\n155\t   - append `workflow.checkout_env` (the three string values) and\n156\t     `workflow.checkout_env_scope`, immediately after unchanged checkout inputs.\n157\t4. `docs/test-reports/windows-p1-stages-20261010/p1-stages.mjs`: **only** the\n158\t   `bindingHash` and `mdHash` 64-character literal values, derived from revised\n159\t   JSON/Markdown. Masking these two values must make all CLI bytes identical to\n160\t   source888. No validator/assertion/guard/import/mode/env/API logic change.\n161\t\n162\tNo new implementation file is allowed. No test, fixture, lockfile, old workflow,\n163\tfrozen runtime, original, state, harness, registry or memory may change. This\n164\tPlanner's only products are this README and `proposal.json` in its own worktree.\n165\t\n166\t### Exact source hashes before the proposed delta\n167\t\n168\t| Path | SHA-256 |\n169\t| --- | --- |\n170\t| P1 workflow | `94aa4fa7b31c49dacb71e2643976314351b7a9ad770b51a6e7d982a344bd962b` |\n171\t| binding Markdown | `bf60ca426602d00b76515091cc30abd37badea21731b6ad21fe54cd323d7577c` |\n172\t| binding JSON | `ed24ebf3b4b1890f84f09ba82edd0d71f75a12e35504a84a3fb0f9d8300455fc` |\n173\t| P1 CLI | `3a2d4174c1b2ac3b0caddb4b10c2ba9146c1569247dc6bd6084be01070a4346b` |\n174\t| unchanged scoped tests | `7718f1e6553f1f9bccca0520571727f2a712493ce789bb8a3f0898a75e289132` |\n175\t\n176\tThe machine-readable before/after strings are normative. Any extra byte, timestamp\n177\tvariation, other literal, alternate env mechanism or wider scope returns to\n178\tPlanner/fresh scope; there is no discretion to expand the candidate.\n179\t\n180\tAuthor-side in-memory rendering of those exact strings yields the following\n181\tprojected SHA-256 values. **None of these source files was edited or executed.**\n182\t\n183\t| Projected file | SHA-256 after the exact proposed delta |\n184\t| --- | --- |\n185\t| P1 workflow | `1ab508fc704fe8ceb1aecbdb9b630ea748add97dc5a17a960940ab4e9a83a771` |\n186\t| binding JSON / new `bindingHash` literal | `652a11170499b8c03bcd70d65ba4f8cdd1476a318e119b267d33cbf90ed1922d` |\n187\t| binding Markdown / new `mdHash` literal | `fc7f4d09915d7200177bf0b4d7c6fc76e95e0423d4e1e2f3f2bc3a1986025ec6` |\n188\t| CLI with only two new identity literals | `3028d77985e965d3de58c965b526bfe6adf7ddebced8b9173c89a5fb6c56e4f6` |\n189\t\n190\t### Validator/import closure and existing test limitations\n191\t\n192\tThis is why the two CLI identity literal changes are unavoidable when revising\n193\tthe locked contract; they are not a native repair exception:\n194\t\n195\t- CLI lines 14-21: JSON SHA must equal `bindingHash` **before import completes**.\n196\t- CLI lines 76-87: `validateBindings()` checks `mdHash`, ten frozen/prior hashes,\n197\t  four scripts/order and the pending-line bound. Only `mdHash` changes.\n198\t- CLI lines 663-686: sourceFiles are eleven dynamically hashed paths. Actual\n199\t  HEAD/scoped-clean source and `validateProvenance()` still enforce bindingHash,\n200\t  source identity, frozen hashes and the unchanged E0 key-name set. No path count,\n201\t  schema or verification rule changes.\n202\t- CLI lines 313-338: fixed environment construction and strict extra-key guard\n203\t  remain byte-identical. Do not admit the checkout keys to native E0.\n204\t- Tests lines 495-503 retain no-spawn/no-write import checks. Lines 536-550 lock\n205\t  original hashes, scripts, E0, ref, commands, timeout, checkout inputs and upload\n206\t  set; they **do not** ban a checkout step env map or hardcode `GIT_CONFIG_*`.\n207\t- Tests lines 552-561 require every entry of the **unchanged**\n208\t  `required_future_controls`. Adding a declared control without adding matching\n209\t  tests would break checks-summary; changing tests/control count is not allowed.\n210\t\n211\tNo remaining source-only validator hardcodes revision 1, an empty existing-file\n212\tallowlist or the original workflow hash. New checkout metadata is a **static\n213\tscope contract**, not a falsely claimed additional runtime validator. Therefore\n214\texisting scoped tests are necessary but insufficient: fresh supporting static\n215\tpositive/negative controls must specifically establish env confinement. The\n216\tsource test assertions were read, not executed here; any historical 64/81 count\n217\tdoes not become new-candidate acceptance by repetition.\n218\t\n219\t## Future checks and gates, all currently unrun\n220\t\n221\t### Before implementation: fresh scope\n222\t\n223\tIndependent fresh supporting critic re-reads both plan files and source888,\n224\thash-checks original inputs and independently renders the exact proposed delta.\n225\tIt must reject disagreement between bindings/proposal, an additional implementation\n226\tpath, a stale source, any native-contract change or a hash-check bypass. Coordinator\n227\tthen explicitly rules on this **four-path** exception. A plan is not a verdict.\n228\t\n229\t### Actual candidate: static and offline supporting acceptance\n230\t\n231\tLet **C** be the actual future immutable full commit SHA, not this docs commit or\n232\tthe moving diagnostic branch. Compare source888 -> C; list report-only files\n233\tseparately. Whole-tree mode/path/blob comparison excluding only the four permitted\n234\tsource paths must preserve every historical archive. The generator handoff must\n235\tinclude exact parent, diff and hashes; workers never push.\n236\t\n237\tRequired static negative fixtures, evaluated in memory or an owned disposable\n238\tsandbox, include:\n239\t\n240\t- missing/false/count0/count2/extra config pairs; non-string values; any added key\n241\t  placed in workflow/job env, later step env, `GITHUB_ENV` or diagnostic child env;\n242\t- global/system/local/worktree config writes, new shell command/probe/version\n243\t  query/retry, sparse/filter/path/defaults/subst, wider events/ref/permissions,\n244\t  Secrets, `continue-on-error` or altered upload boundaries;\n245\t- missing/stale identity literal, one-sided bindings revision, one extra CLI byte,\n246\t  changed test/frozen hash/native script/E0 key/guard/B001 tuple/budget/selection;\n247\t- candidate/HEAD/GITHUB_SHA/source mismatch, dirty source, relabelled old artifact,\n248\t  omitted archive, unsafe provenance or upload. All remain fail-closed.\n249\t\n250\tOffline supporting controls use only owned fixtures, no credentials or PowerShell:\n251\t\n252\t- Documented Git config environment precedence in a child with NOSYSTEM plus an\n253\t  owned empty global config; verify no persistent config entry or sibling-child\n254\t  env contamination. These are disposable tests, **not additional CI probes**.\n255\t- Run the unchanged scoped test file on C with Node22/Vitest, retaining its full\n256\t  output and actual outcomes. Keep import, B001 tuple/source, cleanup/EOF,\n257\t  cap/selection and sealed-artifact negative controls unchanged.\n258\t- Feed the checkout keys to existing `systemEnvironment`: only the five admitted\n259\t  system keys may survive. Inspect fixedEnvironment/strict guard equality without\n260\t  spawning a native process.\n261\t\n262\tEvaluator must be fresh, independent and a **different model family from the\n263\tlater Generator**. It writes supporting `verdict.json` and full raw outputs in\n264\tits own permitted report area. Original verdicts are not rewritten by Planner,\n265\tGenerator or Coordinator. Additional checkout checks remain separate evidence;\n266\tdo not pretend the existing scoped suite already covers them.\n267\t\n268\t### Separate Coordinator publication and one execution gate\n269\t\n270\tAn accepted C still requires explicit Coordinator authority for non-main\n271\tpublication and **one new INITIAL workflow opportunity** on the already-locked\n272\t`codex/windows-p1-stages-ci-20261010` branch. No worker push; no machine writes\n273\t`pending_gate.decision`. This proposal grants neither publication nor execution.\n274\tRerunning source888 cannot execute a changed workflow and is not a repair test.\n275\t\n276\tCapture new final/jobs/artifacts/**full unshortened log** and their hashes; record\n277\tresolved actions. Checkout success must be coupled with the existing prepare\n278\tproving `actual HEAD = C = GITHUB_SHA`, all eleven current source hashes and clean\n279\tscoped source. No added native/version/config inspection command belongs in CI.\n280\t\n281\tThe unchanged workflow may then proceed through prepare, npm ci, scoped checks,\n282\tone INITIAL, seal/verify and its 16-file upload. All four T0-T3 scripts, E0,\n283\told-trace/common guard, API/worker, B001 source closure, selection, caps, budgets\n284\tand quotas remain unchanged (maximum four INITIAL native admissions). Checkout\n285\tgreen alone does not prove even that INITIAL started.\n286\t\n287\tIf checkout/provenance fails, or INITIAL is unknown/refused/incomplete, retain\n288\tthe earliest failure and stop. No automatic retry, extra environment arm,\n289\tPowerShell query or native repair. Missing/empty artifact is no sealed observation;\n290\tif present, independently verify exactly the new sealed set and manifest. New\n291\tnative results are separately evaluated against exact C, never relabelled as\n292\tsource888. F004/F005/release and production/backup gates are not closed by this.\n293\t\n294\t## Author-side boundary and replay\n295\t\n296\tPerformed: disk JSON/log reconciliation and hashes; exact-source workflow,\n297\tbindings, validator/env-test reads; all ten frozen/prior hash checks; current\n298\tgit-tree inventories; official primary documentation inspection. Document\n299\tconsistency checks include unique in-memory substitutions, unchanged locked JSON\n300\tsubtrees/authority flags, projected source hashes and rechecking original hashes;\n301\tthey do not constitute independent scope or functional acceptance.\n302\t\n303\tNot performed: implementation, dependency install, synthetic suite, offline Git\n304\tbehavior test, Windows/native process, CI/rerun, push, production/backup access,\n305\tstate/gate/registry/memory edits or parent worktree index writes. The exact-source\n306\ttask used a new worktree; no pull, remote mutation or shared Git configuration\n307\twrite was necessary or performed. All Git commands used `-c core.fileMode=false`.\n308\t\n309\tReproduce inventories without modifying files:\n310\t\n311\t```sh\n312\tgit -c core.fileMode=false ls-tree -rz --full-tree 888a5acd7a8a441c9ec4ad898453f149cf8d6b7c | shasum -a 256\n313\tgit -c core.fileMode=false ls-tree -rz 888a5acd7a8a441c9ec4ad898453f149cf8d6b7c -- docs/test-reports/windows-native-ci-20261008/runtime-parity-run-37822555762-original | shasum -a 256\n314\t```\n315\t\n316\tAdjacent JSON records complete original hashes, exact proposed workflow/binding\n317\tdeltas, each affected identity check, all future controls and unrun gate fields.\n318\tThose future candidate/verdict/publication/execution fields are **null**, not\n319\timplicit authority. After one exact-path local docs commit and clean/empty index,\n320\tthis supporting Planner stops; Coordinator transports the two artifacts."}
